-- std/secret - Gated secret resolution (M-SECRET-EFFECT, v0.26.0)
--
-- Resolve a secret reference (op://vault/item/field) to its value, gated behind
-- a (possibly remote, human) approval. The reference is safe to pass around and
-- log; the resolved value is labelled <secret> (M-TAINT-TYPES) so the type
-- system forbids it from reaching {not secret} sinks (logs, traces, network
-- bodies) without an explicit ! {Declassify} step.
--
-- Trust model A: resolution runs on the server via the 1Password CLI with a
-- service-account token. Approval is pushed to the operator's device.
--
-- Requires: Secret capability (--caps Secret)

module std/secret

-- secret: Resolve an op:// reference to its plaintext value after approval.
-- The result is labelled <secret> (M-TAINT-TYPES): CheckModuleIFC forbids it
-- from reaching a {not secret} sink without an explicit ! {Declassify} step.
-- `purpose` is the human-readable reason shown in the approval request.
-- Example: let key = secret("op://Prod/stripe/api-key", "charge order #1234")
export func secret(ref: string, purpose: string) -> string<secret> ! {Secret} = _secret_read(ref, purpose)
